{"name":"Light Carob","hex":"#f9dbcf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"carob","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen shrub or tree, Ceratonia siliqua, native to the Mediterranean region.","The fruit of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carob"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carob","blocks":[{"text":"The carob is a flowering evergreen tree or shrub in the Caesalpinioideae subfamily of the legume family, Fabaceae. The carob tree is native to the Mediterranean region and the Middle East. It is widely cultivated for its edible fruit, which takes the form of seed pods, and as an ornamental tree in gardens and landscapes. Spain is its largest producer, followed by Italy and Morocco."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Ceratonia_siliqua_Keciboynuzu_1370984_Nevit.jpg/330px-Ceratonia_siliqua_Keciboynuzu_1370984_Nevit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carob","wikidata":"Q68763"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Carob_tree_leaf.JPG/500px-Carob_tree_leaf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Carob_tree_leaf.JPG/500px-Carob_tree_leaf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A leaflet of the leaf of the carob tree","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarob_tree_leaf.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Illustration_Ceratonia_siliqua0.jpg/500px-Illustration_Ceratonia_siliqua0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Illustration_Ceratonia_siliqua0.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Ceratonia_siliqua0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Illustration_Ceratonia_siliqua0.jpg/500px-Illustration_Ceratonia_siliqua0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of Ceratonia siliqua","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllustration_Ceratonia_siliqua0.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Arcosu07.jpg/500px-Arcosu07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Arcosu07.jpg/1280px-Arcosu07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Arcosu07.jpg/500px-Arcosu07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","al